course: dictionary
lesson: 350
title: Answerable
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Answerable means you have to explain what you did to someone, and take the blame or the credit for it. «The others promised to be answerable for his good conduct» means they promised they would be responsible for how he behaved. The phrase answerable to means you must report to someone, like a pupil answerable to the teacher.
explain: The other meaning is simpler: a question that can be answered is answerable. A riddle with a clear solution is answerable. Ask yourself which meaning fits: is someone asking you to explain yourself, or is something able to be answered?
explain: Look at the words around the word. In «The others promised to be answerable for his good conduct», the word «for» and the word «conduct», which means behaviour, are the clues. Responsibility is the big idea here.
fact: Answerable means having to explain your actions to someone and take responsibility for them.
fact: «Answerable to» means you must report to someone, such as a pupil answerable to a teacher.
fact: «Answerable for» means responsible for something, such as «answerable for his good conduct».
fact: Answerable can also mean able to be answered, as in «an answerable question».
exercise: «The others promised to be answerable for his good conduct.» Here answerable is closest to... | Happy to dance on the grass | Able to be answered in a quiz | *Responsible for how he behaves | Tired and sleepy after the walk
exercise: Mrs Hill asks, «Is this question answerable?» What is she asking? | *Can this question be answered? | Is the question too long to read? | Does the question need a picture? | Is the question about a river?
exercise: «A pupil is answerable to the teacher.» What does this mean? | The pupil is always right | *The pupil must explain their actions to the teacher | The teacher must answer every question the pupil asks | The pupil must sit at the back of the class
test: Dad says, «You are answerable for the dog.» What does he mean? | You must reply whenever the dog barks | You are the only one who can speak to the dog | *You are responsible for looking after the dog
test: «A government is answerable to the people.» What does this mean? | The people must answer the government's phone | *The government must explain its actions to the people | The government never has to say anything to anyone
exam: Which sentence uses answerable to mean able to be answered? | The bridge is answerable to the rain | The jug is answerable and holds two litres | *Her question was answerable, so the teacher replied at once | He was answerable for the sunshine
